14232    !                                         quit;


14233      ods path work.templat(update) sashelp.tmplmst(read);
14234      
14235      data Cheese;
14236      do Additive = 1 to 4;
14237      do y = 1 to 9;
14238      input freq @@;
14239      output;
14240      end;
14241      end;
14242      label y='Taste Rating';
14243      datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.CHEESE has 36 observations and 3 variables.

14248      ;
14249      ods graphics on;
14250      proc logistic data=Cheese plots(only)=oddsratio(range=clip);
14251      freq freq;
14252      class Additive (param=ref ref='4');
14253      model y=Additive / covb nooddsratio;
14254      oddsratio Additive;
14255      effectplot / polybar;
14256      title 'Multiple Response Cheese Tasting Experiment';
14257      run;

NOTE: PROC LOGISTIC is fitting the cumulative logit model. The probabilities modeled are summed over the responses having the lower Ordered Values in the 
      Response Profile table. Use the response variable option DESCENDING if you want to reverse the assignment of Ordered Values to the response levels.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: There were 36 observations read from the data set WORK.CHEESE.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE LOGISTIC printed page 1204.

14258      proc logistic data=Cheese
14259      plots(only)=effect(x=y sliceby=additive connect yrange=(0,0.4));
14260      freq freq;
14261      class Additive (param=ref ref='4');
14262      model y=Additive / nooddsratio link=alogit;
14263      oddsratio Additive;
14264      title 'Multiple Response Cheese Tasting Experiment';
14265      run;

NOTE: PROC LOGISTIC is fitting the adjacent-category logit model. The logits modeled contrast each response level against the next higher Ordered Value. Use 
      the response variable option DESCENDING if you want to contrast higher Ordered Values against lower Ordered Values.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (GCONV=1E-8) satisfied.
NOTE: There were 36 observations read from the data set WORK.CHEESE.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE LOGISTIC printed page 1205.

